# `@: Model m make 3`: a call is its Frame -- `make: 3` or `make(3)` (unit_decl_one_value_call_colon, _call_paren) --
# and `make 3` is two values (the author, 2026-10-06, LMX_blog/2026-10-06.md#explicit-call-frame; the answered
# question LMX_blog/q/value-tail-prefix-call.md).  The declaration takes one value and refuses the second where it
# stands, at 3: "a declaration takes one value" (DECLARATION-CANDIDATE-ROLE).  make returns `Model`, the Structure
# reference its `@: Model` result names.
Model:
    int: value 7
end: Model
fn: make (int: k) @: Model
    return: Model
end: make
fn: check () int
    @: Model m make 3
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
